# The Vitesse Deepgreen DB 18.16 Software License Agreement, which the
# installer requires you to accept, contains a DeWitt clause. Section 3.3:
# "Customer agrees not to: ... (iii) disclose results of any benchmark tests
# related to the Software without VITESSE DATA's prior written consent."
# The same section limits use to "a single Node for a period of thirty (30)
# days for EVALUATION purpose only".
#
# So this entry follows the ClickBench rule for results that cannot be
# published (top-level README, "If The Results Cannot Be Published", and the
# kdb entry): the reproduction scripts are here in full, the numbers are not.
# Anyone can run ./benchmark.sh and get them for themselves.
results/

# ./install downloads the vendor's installer here and deletes it again when
# it is done. Section 3.1 of the same licence forbids making the Software
# "available in any form to anyone other than Customer's" own people, so make
# sure a failed install can never leave it staged for a commit.
deepgreendb.*.bin
dg-layer.tar.gz
hits.tsv
